    "uncertainCells": [],
    "notes": "Advanced side of the classic-typeface 1961 printing, named '-orig' to pair with that basic card (the modern 1961 back is batter_virdon-bill_1961). The 972x1600 back scan shows two copies of this classic back (green ink at the top, blue ink in the middle) above the modern back; transcribed from 1.9x half-card crops of the green copy, then independently re-read from the blue copy, which agrees cell for cell. Source: a 2019 collector's post of his Bill Virdon Strat-O-Matic cards (Wayback capture). It differs from the modern 1961 back in e-rating (e7 vs e6), shares (31/69 on both) and the whole grid arrangement. '?' after fly balls (printed 'B ?') captured as questionMark. Hit locations print with no space ('DOUBLE(cf)'), kept verbatim. 'plus injury' on LHP col2 r12 and RHP col3 r2."
  }
